      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the probability that when rolling four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show the same number, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of possible outcomes when rolling four dice.\n2. Determine the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number.\n3. Subtract the number of unfavorable outcomes from the total number of outcomes to get the number of favorable outcomes.\n4. Calculate the probability by dividing the number of favorable outcomes by the total number of possible outcomes.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of possible outcomes.**\n\nEach die has 6 faces, and since we are rolling four dice, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n\\[6 \\times 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 6^4 = 1296.\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number.**\n\nThere are 6 possible outcomes where all four dice show the same number (one for each number from 1 to 6). So, the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number is:\n\\[6.\\]\n\n**Step 3: Subtract the number of unfavorable outcomes from the total number of outcomes.**\n\nThe number of favorable outcomes (where not all four dice show the same number) is the total number of outcomes minus the number of unfavorable outcomes:\n\\[1296 - 6 = 1290.\\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the probability.**\n\nThe probability that all four dice do not show the same number is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n\\[\\frac{1290}{1296} = \\frac{215}{216}.\\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show the same number is:\n\\[\\boxed{\\frac{215}{216}}.\\]",
