      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show the same number, we can start by calculating the total number of possible outcomes and then subtract the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number.\n\n1. **Total number of outcomes**: \n   Each die has 6 faces, and since we are rolling 4 dice, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 6^4 = 1296\n   \\]\n\n2. **Number of favorable outcomes**: \n   For the dice not to all show the same number, at least two of the dice must show different numbers. We can break this down into the cases where exactly two dice show the same number and the other two dice show different numbers.\n\n   - **Case 1: Exactly two dice show the same number and the other two show different numbers**:\n     - Choose the number that appears twice (6 choices).\n     - Choose 2 out of the 4 dice to show this number ( \\(\\binom{4}{2} = 6\\) ways).\n     - Choose the number for the other two dice (5 choices, since it must be different from the number on the pair of dice).\n     - The number of ways to assign these numbers to the 4 dice is:\n       \\[\n       6 \\times 6 \\times 5 \\times 4 = 720\n       \\]\n\n   - **Case 2: All four dice show the same number**:\n     - There are 6 possible outcomes (one for each number from 1 to 6).\n\n   However, we have double-counted the cases where all four dice show the same number (since it is included in both the \"exactly two dice show the same number\" and the \"all four dice show the same number\" cases). There are 6 such cases.\n\n   Therefore, the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number is 6. The number of outcomes where exactly two dice show the same number and the other two dice show different numbers is:\n   \\[\n   720 - 6 = 714\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total number of favorable outcomes**:\n   The total number of favorable outcomes is:\n   \\[\n   714 + 6 = 720\n   \\]\n\n4. **Probability**:\n   The probability that the four dice will not all show the same number is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1296 - 720}{1296} = \\frac{576}{1296} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show the same number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]",
